## Pure rational case cuts · `sec:cas:decision-cuts`

`Cas::check_case_cut(&CaseCut,&mut Budget)` checks only whether the supplied rational box lies in an existing native association and its case domain. `CaseCut` retains the exact function and association handles, ordered `CoordinateInterval` records and an optional `IntegerCellRange`. Coordinates must be distinct closed Real declarations under the exact case header; a Real-axis box has that axis, and an Assignments box includes every declared Real coordinate. Reversed intervals, missing axes, foreign handles, changed headers and an association absent from the function refuse. Every endpoint comparison uses exact `Rational` arithmetic.

The checker reconstructs dense affine coefficients for rational literals, coordinates, negation, addition, subtraction, multiplication by a constant and division by a nonzero constant. It evaluates each coordinate coefficient at its sign-directed endpoints. Positive, nonnegative, equality and nonzero predicates retain their strict boundary conventions; zero requires the whole affine range to equal zero. Constant integer predicates, total Boolean constructors, ambient/empty regions, guards, meet, union and difference use conservative whole-box truth. A union succeeds when a member covers the complete box; the checker does not subdivide a box to prove a union cover. All original dependencies are checked, including undefined or unsupported operands beneath a zero multiplier.

**Rule (Integral rational case cut)** · `rule:cas:decision-cut-integer`

An integer-cell question requires an exactly integral Real rational arm literal n, membership of n in the supplied exact integer range, and `n <= lower <= upper < n+1` on the named coordinate. Missing range endpoints are exact absent bounds. This establishes no `Integer`-sorted case result: ordinary native scalar associations still reject that sort (`test:integration:decision-cut-integer-result-remains-unsupported`). The checked finite partition interface authenticates the declared option/range association before a cut is reused under that contract (`rule:cas:decision-partition-integer`).

`DecisionBoundaryIntersection` reports a box without uniform established membership; `DecisionOutsideRegion` reports uniform exclusion. Malformed boxes and option/range mismatches have distinct typed codes. Unsupported predicates, named provenance, nonlinear syntax, variable divisors, placements and non-rational cuts return `UnsupportedCertificate`. An exact separating lemma for a non-rational boundary remains unsupported by this subset. A finite radius or inward-rounded endpoint has no enclosure authority here; the missing enclosure-origin checker must establish that the original target belongs to the supplied box.

**Rule (Pure case-cut lifecycle)** · `rule:cas:decision-cut-lifecycle`

The operation leaves graph occupancy unchanged on success and refusal, returns no witness or hypothesis, and uses no cache. It charges its own traversal and exact arithmetic on the caller's cumulative ledger, retaining spent Work on refusal. The input box and dependency plan reserve staged bytes before allocation. Completed coefficient vectors reserve their measured rational payload, while one new vector and bounded scalar scratch reserve the component-ceiling bound; retained graph and output bytes are zero. The existing formal register, primitive manifest, wire format and ordinary selection route are unchanged. Certified local introduction, expected-judgment replay, richer partitions and source-family premises remain open at the partition authority boundary (`rule:cas:decision-partition-authority`).

Independent cut fixtures cover integer cells (`test:integration:decision-cut-integer-cell`), all three sign regions (`test:integration:decision-cut-sign-regions`), the upper-left chart and owned real axis (`test:integration:decision-cut-phase-chart`), affine cancellation and coordinate extrema (`test:integration:decision-cut-affine-predicates`), unsupported certificates (`test:integration:decision-cut-unsupported-certificates`), exact identities and box shape (`test:integration:decision-cut-identities-and-boxes`), scope and domain (`test:integration:decision-cut-scope-and-domain`) and the read-only lifecycle (`test:integration:decision-cut-read-only-lifecycle`).

The integer, sign and upper-left cut fixtures have literal measured resource boundaries under the unchanged rational component ceilings:

|Cut fixture|Work|Minimum staged bytes|Added graph bytes|Output bytes|Cache calls|
|-----------|----|--------------------|-----------------|------------|-----------|
|Integer cell|11,670|51,736|0|0|0|
|Negative sign|4,721|47,728|0|0|0|
|Upper-left chart|9,356|54,992|0|0|0|

The staged figures are conservative allowance thresholds, not allocator measurements. Exact N/N−1 tests cover Work and staging, one unit of prior Work, a retained input byte and restoration of temporary limits (`test:integration:decision-cut-resource-boundaries`). Repeating a cut costs the same Work on the cumulative ledger; an exhausted third attempt leaves usage and graph occupancy unchanged (`test:integration:decision-cut-cumulative-ledger`). These are cut-only costs and exclude target enclosure replay, partition admission and certified-membership introduction.

## Checked finite decision partitions · `sec:cas:decision-partitions`

**Definition (Checked finite decision contract)** · `def:cas:decision-partition-contract`

`CasePartition` identifies one immutable native function, ordered Real coordinate handles and an optional finite `IntegerCellRange`. `Cas::check_case_partition(&CasePartition,&mut Budget)` checks the complete actual association inventory and returns a privately constructed `CheckedCasePartition` only after finite partition admission (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`). Its `contract()` method borrows the retained exact input and `retained_bytes()` reports the conservative logical ownership bound.

**Rule (Finite decision partition admission)** · `rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`

The checker validates the case domain, exact header and closed scope, every ambient Real coordinate and every original predicate operand. It reconstructs rational affine coefficients and accepts each comparison only when at most one coordinate coefficient remains after exact cancellation. Sorted rational cuts induce a finite Cartesian partition into open intervals, rays and singleton boundaries. Every cell inside the nonempty declared domain must have exactly one option; every cell outside it must have none. Native Boolean region constructors combine these total predicates. This checks explicit boundary ownership, complete cover and pairwise disjointness for the retained contract (`def:cas:decision-partition-contract`), including the sign trichotomy and all seven phase-chart regions.

**Rule (Finite integer decision family)** · `rule:cas:decision-partition-integer`

An integer partition declaration requires both finite integral endpoints and exactly one matching Real coordinate. Admission checks each original integral Real option literal, its exact half-open unit cell and equality of the case domain with the declared range, in addition to complete partition admission (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`). The five-cell fixture declares `[0,5)`. This supplies neither an `Integer`-sorted native result nor a parametric or unbounded family (`test:integration:decision-partition-integer-contract`).

**Rule (Finite partition refusals)** · `rule:cas:decision-partition-refusals`

Removing any partition member, including zero or an owned phase axis, refuses with `CoverageHole`; overlaps refuse with `DecisionPartitionOverlap` even when the arm values agree. `DecisionPartitionOutsideDomain` refuses an option extending beyond the domain, and empty domains refuse. These follow from the exhaustive ownership test (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`). Oblique affine comparisons, nonlinear predicates, non-rational cuts, variable divisors, partial or named predicates, placements and scope transports remain `UnsupportedCertificate` or a scope refusal; none acquires authority from its name or from an unreachable Boolean branch.

**Rule (Sealed partition reuse)** · `rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`

A caller retains one `CheckedCasePartition` per immutable case revision (`def:cas:decision-partition-contract`). `Cas::check_partition_cut(&CheckedCasePartition,&CaseCut,&mut Budget)` checks the same store, function, ordered axes and integer range, then checks the current box cut. It does not reconstruct the complete partition. Explicitly calling `check_case_partition` again performs and charges another full check; there is no global or ledger cache, and no cache hit or miss. Handles share immutable graph syntax, while the returned value owns its coordinate vector and integer bounds. Reuse retains that contract throughout the current cut calculation (`rule:cas:decision-cut-lifecycle`).

**Rule (Partition authority boundary)** · `rule:cas:decision-partition-authority`

The sealed partition is a prerequisite calculation, not a `VerifiedWitness`, local hypothesis or portable cover lemma. It has no wire encoding and cannot enter case elimination. Rational enclosure replay for the original target and admitted input family, the certified-membership kind and introduction lemma, retained source assumptions and the sign-to-nonzero consequence remain open. A valid negative cut under a checked partition still leaves the original reciprocal's `NonZero` premise open (`test:integration:decision-partition-no-membership-authority`). Existing formal registration, proof selection, wire and budget defaults retain their behavior and costs.

**Procedure (Finite partition conformance)** · `alg:cas:decision-partition-conformance`

Independent public tests cover complete examples (`test:integration:decision-partition-complete-examples`), every missing member (`test:integration:decision-partition-missing-members`), overlap and domain ownership (`test:integration:decision-partition-overlap-and-domain`), integer declaration mismatches (`test:integration:decision-partition-integer-contract`), sealed reuse (`test:integration:decision-partition-qualified-reuse`), unsupported or undefined predicates (`test:integration:decision-partition-total-predicates`), rational shifted boundaries and exact cancellation (`test:integration:decision-partition-affine-boundaries`), native Boolean regions (`test:integration:decision-partition-boolean-regions`), coordinate identity (`test:integration:decision-partition-coordinate-identities`) and the absence of membership authority (`test:integration:decision-partition-no-membership-authority`). These exercise the exact admission and refusal rules (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`), (`rule:cas:decision-partition-refusals`).

**Example (Finite integer partition costs)** · `ex:cas:decision-partition-integer-costs`

Five integer cells over `[0,5)` require 165,692 Work, 77,288 staged bytes and 524 returned bytes for admission, with 13 exact cells. Reusing that contract with the worked cycle box costs 23,132 Work and 58,076 staged bytes. These are the finite integer declaration and reuse lifecycles (`rule:cas:decision-partition-integer`), (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`), pinned by literal resource tests (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`), (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`).

**Example (Sign partition costs)** · `ex:cas:decision-partition-sign-costs`

The sign trichotomy requires 17,140 Work, 52,332 staged bytes and 192 returned bytes for admission, with three exact cells. Reusing that contract with the worked negative box costs 5,388 Work and 47,920 staged bytes. These are the complete admission and reuse lifecycles (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`), (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`), pinned by literal resource tests (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`), (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`).

**Example (Phase partition costs)** · `ex:cas:decision-partition-phase-costs`

The seven phase charts require 48,944 Work, 67,112 staged bytes and 256 returned bytes for admission, with nine exact Cartesian cells. Reusing that contract with the upper-left rectangle costs 10,420 Work and 55,248 staged bytes. These are the complete admission and reuse lifecycles (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`), (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`), pinned by literal resource tests (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`), (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`).

**Rule (Finite partition resource ownership)** · `rule:cas:decision-partition-resources`

Work and staging cover traversal, total affine reconstruction, exact cuts, cell ownership and retained copies. Returned and caller-retained bytes are the same bound; added graph bytes and reuse output are zero. Reuse staging includes the retained contract plus the full current box-cut scratch (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`). These thresholds are conservative accounted bounds, not allocator measurements. Literal N/N−1 tests pin admission Work, staging, output and Cartesian cells, prior Work and one retained input byte (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`); reuse Work, staging and cumulative exhaustion (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`); and combined admission/reuse with atomic refusal and a widened box (`test:integration:decision-partition-atomic-lifecycle`). No permanent test searches a byte threshold, and spent Work remains spent on refusal.
